BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23234Z
UID:B672tifsnu-8220440229@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260602T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260602T200000
SUMMARY:Author of new book on Don Bolles assassination headlines 50th anniversary commemoration
URL:http://bit.ly/48LW3s9
DESCRIPTION:Fifty years ago\, a Phoenix reporter lost his life when someone planted a bomb beneath his car and detonated it as he backed out of a parking space at a local hotel. What exactly happened to The Arizona Republic’s Don Bolles on June 2\, 1976\, and why\, continues to fascinate the journalism profession\, the state and nation five decades later.

Join Valley of the Sun SPJ as we gather the local media community to commemorate the life\, career and death of this dedicated journalist at Baseline Flowers\, 3801 E. Baseline Road\, Phoenix. Admission is free\, but RSVPs are requested at https://bit.ly/48LW3s9

Hear local journalist Jeremy Duda of Axios Phoenix\, author of a new book about the Bolles assassination\, “Murder in the Fourth Estate\,” and Republic reporter Richard Ruelas\, who has written extensively about Bolles. Also on the panel is George Weisz\, who as a graduate journalism student worked on a comprehensive journalistic investigation into Bolles’ death\, The Arizona Project. Later\, while with the Arizona Attorney General’s Office\, Weisz prosecuted two of the three defendants accused on Bolles’ murder.

Light refreshments will be served. Duda said he will bring copies of the book to sell and autograph at this event.
LOCATION:3801 East Baseline Road\, Phoenix\, AZ\, USA
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23235Z
UID:klTx3X17nt-8222596849@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260602
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260605
SUMMARY:79th Annual EWA National Seminar
URL:http://ewa.org/events/upcoming-events/2026-education-writers-association-national-seminar
DESCRIPTION:The Education Writers Association (EWA) will hold its 2026 National Seminar in Baltimore\, Maryland\, June 2-5\, 2026. Scholarships are available to journalists covering education\, whether full-time on the beat or for a particular investigation\, series or story. (We are currently offering journalists impacted by layoffs and newsroom cuts priority consideration for scholarships covering registration.)

The 79th annual National Seminar will follow seismic changes to education at the federal level\, including huge staffing cuts in the U.S. Department of Education\, the loss of federal funding for research at universities and an overhaul of the student loan system. Meanwhile\, schools\, educators and students face ongoing challenges -- from inequitable resources to declining enrollment -- while navigating emerging trends\, such as significant growth among workforce development programs and the use of artificial intelligence. 

EWA will use this unprecedented moment to help members understand how stakeholders are affected amid major shifts in federal oversight and funding while also providing training and offering solutions on how to best cover persistent education issues. Sessions focusing on journalism skills -- from best FOIA request practices to effectively using archival material in coverage --will also be a key part of the conference. 
LOCATION:401 West Pratt Street\, Baltimore\, Maryland 21201\, USA
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23236Z
UID:QCeXOh5Urf-8221280016@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260604T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260604T190000
SUMMARY:Freelancing with ADHD: Productivity Strategies That Actually Work
URL:http://calendar.spjnetwork.org/displayevent.php?e=QCeXOh5Urf-8221280016
DESCRIPTION:RSVP is required at spjfreelancecommunity@gmail.com
Thursday\, June 4\, 2026 at 6pm ET

The SPJ Freelance Community has launched a workshop for journalist coping with ADHD. We invite you to join us for “Freelancing with ADHD: Productivity Strategies That Actually Work\,” a virtual\, hands-on training offered by expert\, Jen Brdlik\, who is focused on providing proven strategies to help you succeed.

Jen Brdlik\, MSW\, LMT\, BCTMB\, is neurodivergent life coach\, former mental health therapist\, and an ADHD and autism specialist.

Some neurodivergent journalists find themselves distracted in a world of chaos\, especially when their brain is wired
differently. The struggle is real. Even if you’re disciplined\, your brain may find that it is difficult to balance many things while on assignment.

It’s not unusual for a freelance journalist to pitch stories to an editor\, research topics\, track down subject matter experts\, deal with deadlines\, all while working on multiple assignments at once.

Whether you’re a full-time or part-time freelance journalist overwhelmed or on the verge of burnout\, this session will help you assess difficulties\, deal with pressure and offer tips to keep you calm while you thrive and achieve clarity and control.

RSVP is required at spjfreelancecommunity@gmail.com

LOCATION:
END:VEVENT





